# The pin archive sets (compile-speed plan §3.3; docs/spec/build.md, Pin
# archives): what a pin would otherwise compile on each machine, built once
# and shipped as a download. A set line names a set (internal/pinset,
# Key.Name: kind, Go release, target, and a digest of the whole key: the
# release, the IR patch, the flags and the target) and the sha256 of its
# tar. ergo uses a fetched set only when its sha256 is this one; any other
# set, or none, is built once on the machine instead, to the same bytes.
# `go run ./scripts/pinsets -lock` makes the sets and rewrites this file;
# TestPinArchivesMatchLocalBuild checks that a local build makes these
# exact sets.
